# Nothing here is required. A new install asks its password, language and
# time zone in the dashboard the first time it is opened; what to watch, where
# to notify and how to behave are set there too and kept in the database.
# Copy this file to .env only for something the dashboard does not set.
#
# Do not write comments after a value on the same line.

# The password, set here instead of in the dashboard, which then cannot
# change it. Without it, the password is chosen in the dashboard, and
#   docker compose exec quotapulse /quotapulse reset-password
# prints a link to choose a new one.
# QUOTAPULSE_PASSWORD=

# Encrypts stored credentials. Optional: when unset, a random key is created
# in the data directory on first start (data/secret.key). Set it if you would
# rather keep the key out of the data directory — and never change it
# afterwards, or stored credentials can no longer be read.
# QUOTAPULSE_SECRET=

# Time zone and language (en or zh) for a NEW install, which the dashboard
# otherwise asks when it is set up. Both can be changed there later.
# TZ=Asia/Shanghai
# QUOTAPULSE_LANG=zh

# A bundle to import when the database is empty: a declarative way to start
# with accounts, dates and channels already in place. See docs/bundle.md.
# QUOTAPULSE_BOOTSTRAP=/data/bootstrap.json

# 1 records notifications without sending them. Useful while checking a
# migration: the Activity page shows what would have gone out.
# QUOTAPULSE_MUTE=1

# Logging: text or json; debug, info, warn or error.
# QUOTAPULSE_LOG=json
# QUOTAPULSE_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Docker Compose only.
#
# Where the dashboard is published on the host: a port, or address:port to
# keep it on loopback behind a reverse proxy on the same machine.
# QUOTAPULSE_PORT=8080
# QUOTAPULSE_PORT=127.0.0.1:8080
#
# The release to hold. Without it, the 1.x line: a pull brings the newest 1.x.
# QUOTAPULSE_VERSION=1.2.2
#
# Another image altogether - a fork, a mirror - instead of the published one.
# QUOTAPULSE_IMAGE=
#
# The user to start as. Without it the container starts as root, only to take
# ./data over, and runs as whoever owns it (65532 for a new one).
# QUOTAPULSE_USER=1000:1000
